From 508b2ab67ae3a1475504832d6184f6a527a5de23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 14:24:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add CHD disc image support

Load Xbox disc images stored as MAME CHD (chdman createdvd, or createcd with
one data track), read compressed through libchdr as the game runs.

- block/chd.c: a read-only block driver for the DVD drive. libchdr reads
  through the driver's file child, in windows of the file, and decodes on the
  thread pool, so the main loop and the lock the emulated CPU needs are not
  held while a hunk is decompressed; 16 MiB of decoded hunks are kept.
- block/chd-disc.c: the disc's layout in a CHD, with no QEMU in it: chdman's
  DVD layout (flat 2048-byte units) and a CD's (MODE1 or MODE1_RAW track).
- libchdr as a static CMake subproject (miniz, lzma and zstd come with it).
- ui: xemu_load_disc opens a .chd with the chd driver (the boot drive has no
  format, and finds it by its header); the file dialog and the games list
  take .chd.

Based on the block driver of pull request 2809, reworked.
